        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260529-live-nato-condemns-russia-s-recklessness-after-drone-hit-apartment-building-in-romania",
        "orario": "07:45",
        "timestamp": 1780033530,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Live Live: NATO condemns 'Russia's recklessness' after drone hit apartment building in Romania Europe Issued on: 29/05/2026 - 07:42 Modified: 29/05/2026 - 08:23 NATO on Friday condemned 'Russia's recklessness' after a drone launched as part of an overnight attack on Ukraine crashed into an apartment building in eastern Romania. At least two people were injured, and a fire was ignited after the incident, according to local authorities. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates. 29/05/2026 - 08:21 US anti-drone system 'operational' but too risky to use in city, Romania says The US ​anti-drone system Merops is ​operational in Romania, but would have been too risky to ​use ‌in ⁠a city, Romanian Brigadier General ‌Gheorghe Maxim said on Friday ⁠after a drone hit the roof ​of a block ‌of flats and caused an explosion. 29/05/2026 - 08:08 Romania condemns 'grave and irresponsible escalation from Russia' NATO will strengthen defences against threats, including drones Fuel storage facilities on fire in Russia's Yaroslavl region after drone attack, governor says Russian drone strike damaged Turkish ship sailing from Odesa, Ukraine navy says Russian drones attacked three foreign-flagged vessels, Ukraine's deputy PM says 29/05/2026 - 08:08 Moldova president says 'Russia is a danger to all' after 'grave' Romania drone strike The president of Moldova, sandwiched between Ukraine and Romania, condemned a \"grave\" Russian drone strike that wounded two people in Romania. \"I strongly condemn Russian drones striking Romanians in their homes,\" Maia Sandu said on X. \"This is grave. The Republic of Moldova stands in full solidarity with Romania and wishes a swift recovery to those injured in Galati. Russia is a danger to all and must be stopped.\" 29/05/2026 - 08:08 Russian drones attacked three foreign-flagged vessels, Ukraine's deputy PM says Russian ⁠drones ​attacked three foreign-flagged ​merchant vessels late on Thursday ​and ‌overnight on ⁠Friday as ‌they were moving ⁠along Ukraine's export maritime corridor ​in the ‌Black Sea, Deputy Prime ‌Minister Oleksiy ​Kuleba said. The strikes caused fires to break ​out on ​board the ​vessels, which were ​extinguished by the crews, Kuleba said ⁠on Telegram. 29/05/2026 - 08:03 Romania general says drone was in Romania for 4 minutes 29/05/2026 - 07:57 'Russia's war of aggression has crossed yet another line', von der Leyen says European ⁠Commission President ​Ursula von der ​Leyen said Russia had \"crossed yet ​another line\" ‌after one ⁠of its drones ‌hit a densely populated ⁠area in Romania and injured civilians during ​an overnight attack ‌in neighbouring Ukraine. \"We stand in full solidarity ‌with Romania and ​its people,\" von der Leyen said in a post ​on X. \"As we ​continue strengthening our ​security and deterrence, especially ​on our eastern border, we will keep increasing the pressure ⁠on Russia.\" 29/05/2026 - 07:53 Russian drone strike damaged Turkish ship sailing from Odesa, Ukraine navy says Ukraine's navy said that a Russian drone strike sparked a fire on a cargo ship bound for Turkey that had departed the Ukrainian port of Odesa. \"The Russian Federation carried out a targeted attack on a Turkish vessel,\" the Ukrainian navy posted on Telegram saying a fire had broken out and two crew members wounded on the Vanuatu-flagged cargo vessel, which had Turkish owners. 29/05/2026 - 07:52 Fuel storage facilities on fire in Russia's Yaroslavl region after drone attack, governor says Fuel ⁠storage ​facilities caught ​fire following a Ukraine drone attack in ​Russia's ‌Yaroslavl ⁠region, northeast of ‌Moscow, Governor Mikhail Yevrayev ⁠said on Telegram, adding that work ​to extinguish ‌the fire were ongoing. Overall, ‌Russia downed 208 ​drones overnight, Interfax said, citing the defense ministry. ​Of ​those, over ​80 were shot ​down in Russia's southern Rostov region, local authorities ⁠said. 29/05/2026 - 07:44 Drone incident reflects Russian threat to European security, French minister says ⁠French Minister ​for European Affairs Benjamin Haddad said ​on Friday that an incident involving a Russian drone in Romania showed ​that ‌Russia was ⁠a threat to European security. \"Russia has not only attacked Ukraine, but ‌also threatened the European security architecture. A ​Russian drone crashed in Romania again last night, posing a threat through ​its interference,\" Haddad told French ​radio RMC. \"I would ​also like to point out that we ​have French troops stationed in Romania as part of NATO's reassurance operations, specifically to demonstrate our ⁠support for the sovereignty of our partners in ⁠Europe,\" ​he added. 29/05/2026 - 07:41 NATO will strengthen defences against threats, including drones ⁠NATO ⁠said it ​would strengthen ​its defences against all threats, including drones, after ​a ‌drone crashed ⁠onto the roof ‌of a 10-storey block ⁠of flats in the southeastern Romanian ​city of ‌Galati during a Russian overnight attack on ‌neighbouring Ukraine. \"We condemn ​Russia's recklessness, and NATO will continue to strengthen our ​defences against ​all threats, ​including drones,\" a NATO spokesperson ​said in a post on social media platform ⁠X. 29/05/2026 - 07:40 Romania condemns 'grave and irresponsible escalation from Russia' ⁠The ​Romanian Ministry ​of Foreign Affairs said on Friday that ​an ‌incident ⁠involving a Russian ‌drone that struck an ⁠apartment building in a ​Romanian city is ‌a \"grave and irresponsible escalation ‌from Russia\". \"Romania has ​informed allies and NATO's secretary general about ​the circumstances ​and requested measures to accelerate ​the transfer of anti-drone capabilities to Romania,\" the ⁠ministry said. 29/05/2026 - 07:37 Russian drone launched against Ukraine crashes in Romania, injuring two A Russian drone that was part of an overnight attack on Ukraine crashed into an apartment building in eastern Romania, injuring two people, Romanian authorities said Friday. 29/05/2026 - 07:33 Welcome to the France 24 liveblog covering the Ukraine war. Catch up on yesterday's latest happenings here . (FRANCE 24 with AFP, AP and Reuters)"
